	(paper "A4")
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "POWER-SHEET CRITICAL NOTES\nBATTERY: Use only a protected 1S Li-ion battery pack. Verify connector keying and polarity before assembly or power application.\nREV-A LIMITATION: The 2-wire battery pack provides no thermistor connection. TS is fixed-biased and does not provide actual battery-temperature monitoring.\n\nFIRMWARE: At every charger initialization, program BQ25895 REG04 ICHG to 1.024 A and verify the applicable input-current-limit policy.\n\nCAPACITORS: MLCC values shown are nominal. Use X5R or X7R dielectric at the specified voltage rating and verify effective capacitance at the operating DC bias for every selected MPN.\nPOWER SEQUENCE: Assert BOOST_5V_EN before USB_HOST_VBUS_EN. Disable USB_HOST_VBUS_EN before disabling BOOST_5V_EN.\nGROUNDING: CHG_PGND is a local high-current return, not a separate board ground plane. Connect it to the common GND at the charger PowerPAD/current-loop region through the designated net tie.\nNOISE CONTROL: Keep charger, buck-boost and boost switch nodes and current loops away from GNSS, UWB, RF matching networks, antennas and reference clocks.\nFIRST POWER-UP: Use a current-limited bench supply. Check resistance to GND and verify VSYS, +3V3, +5V_SYS and VBUS_HOST individually before connecting final loads or the battery."
